Note the last seven rows: CPU utilization fell to 21-41% (well under the 60% target) by
7m33s, but replicas held at 10 for the remainder of this capture (through 9m18s, i.e.
~1m45s of sustained under-threshold utilization and counting) — the scaleDown
stabilizationWindowSeconds: 300 in k8s/base/hpa.yaml deliberately keeping capacity up
rather than flapping back down immediately. A longer capture would show the scale-down
completing once the full 300s window elapses without a new high reading.
